# Visualization.

**Authors:** Williams, James G., And Others

## Abstract
Provides a background on the use of the digital computer to support visualization in scientific computing (scientific visualization). Includes an example of scientific and nonscientific visualization. Reviews both scientific and other visualization research literature; development; and applications organized around a model of visualization components that include data, models, the computing system, interface, and users. Contains 84 references. (AEF)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ518328

